Date: Sun, 5 Sep 93 23:56:15 PDT
From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: SF: Vernor Vinge Wins Hugo for "A Fire Upon the Deep"

As the title says, Vinge won the Huge for Best Novel.

Actually, it _tied_ with Connie Willis's "The Doomsday Book." But a
win is a win.

"A Fire Upon the Deep" was extensively praised by many of us on this
list some months back, hence the relevance of this announcement.

At Worldcon, I shared a panel (on "Ethics and Computers") with Jean
Gawron, author of "Dreams of Glass." Expecting to meet him on the
panel, I set out to read this novel beginning just before the Con. I'm
now at the half-way point, having been gone the past several days.

So far, it is outstanding, in a league with "Snow Crash" as a
portrayal of cyberspace and the Net (though with a different cant that
any of the "standard works" on cyberspace).

Gawron is very interested, by the way, in the cypherpunkish kind of
stuff, and wants to talk about crypto anarchy some more. He's local
(in the AI group at SRI in Menlo Park, CA), so this looks promising.

-Tim May
